Aether: webrtc/search tail

Third-party relocation, WebRTC using declarations, search detection, backend C++, l10n handler, Nimbus/Mach/WebRTC telemetry.

Squashed from 8 units:

  [core/64-thirdparty-relocation.patch]
  Aether: move the untrusted-modules API onto nsIAboutThirdParty
  
  about:thirdparty is deliberately kept, but it reached its data
  through nsITelemetry, which is about to be deleted. The two methods
  and four flags move onto the page's own nsIAboutThirdParty interface
  (values unchanged), implemented in AboutThirdParty.cpp by delegating
  to the existing UntrustedModules collector, and the page reads them
  off its own service instead of Services.telemetry.
  
  [core/65-webrtc-using.patch]
  Aether: remove the orphaned Telemetry using in PeerConnectionImpl
  
  PeerConnectionImpl carried an orphaned `using namespace Telemetry;`
  whose recording code is long gone; it only survived on unified-build
  include leakage and broke the build once the TU stood alone. The
  WebRTC call-telemetry shells themselves go in a follow-up.
  
  [core/66-search-detection-perm.patch]
  Aether: drop the orphaned telemetry permission
  
  The built-in search-detection extension still declared the
  "telemetry" permission, which no longer validates since the
  browser.telemetry API went away (patch 50). Its code never used it.
  
  [core/67-backend-cpp.patch]
  Aether: delete the legacy telemetry C++ backend
  
  The legacy telemetry C++ backend goes in one atomic cut: the core
  recorders, the IPC accumulation layer, the YAML probe tables with
  their generated-header rules, the GIFFT map generation, nsITelemetry
  itself with its XPCOM registration, the six-message IPC blocks with
  both Recv and Send sides, the release-data Init params (child
  untrusted-module processors now start unconditionally, as they
  already did everywhere else), the XPCOM init hooks, the late-write
  checker with its shutdown-phase plumbing, the profile-dir handoff,
  pingsender with its packaging entry, and the product-side recording
  call sites in layout, netwerk, IPC launchers and media (keeping every
  functional behavior: checkerboard tracking state, input-time stats,
  cache flows). about:thirdparty was moved onto its own interface
  beforehand and keeps working.
  
  [core/68-l10n-onchange-handler.patch]
  Aether: swallow the expected l10n retranslation rejection
  
  Switching the application locale re-translates every open document via
  DOMLocalization::OnChange -> TranslateRoots. A resource that is missing
  from the newly selected locale (e.g. the es-ES langpack ships neither
  browser/preferences/clearSiteData.ftl nor browser/allTabsMenu.ftl) leaves
  elements untranslated, which rejects the root promise with no value. That
  promise had no observer, so every language switch printed a bare
  "uncaught exception: undefined" to the console.
  
  Attach an empty native handler that discards the result. Nothing can act
  on a failed re-translation, and document.l10n.ready deliberately resolves
  in the very same situation (L10nReadyHandler in DocumentL10n.cpp), so
  reporting it as uncaught was noise, not signal. The per-resource
  "Missing resource in locale ..." diagnostics are unaffected.
  
  Verified with a headless Marionette repro (open about:preferences, set
  Services.locale.requestedLocales to es-ES): before, one uncaught
  exception; after, the rejection is consumed and the console stays clean.
  Windows build green, 0 warnings.
  
  [core/69-nimbus-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: kill the last Nimbus telemetry writers
  
  Kill the last FOG writers in the Nimbus unit. Enrollment logic is untouched.
  
  - lib/Telemetry.sys.mjs: drop Services.fog.setExperimentActive /
    setExperimentInactive, the now-dead experiment-type constants and the
    unused FirstStartup import. What remains are the enrollment reason
    enums (consumed by live enrollment logic in six modules) plus empty
    record*/setExperimentActive shells so no call site changes.
  - lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs: drop the nimbusTelemetry onUpdate
    block whose only effect was Services.fog.applyServerKnobsConfig.
  
  Exposure recording was already neutered (recordExposureEvent only flips
  a flag; the C++ RecordExposureEvent resolves metadata and returns), and
  TargetingContextRecorder is empty shells, so after this no Nimbus code
  writes telemetry anywhere.
  
  [core/70-mach-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: kill mach invocation telemetry
  
  Kill mach invocation telemetry, including the startup and shutdown
  paths the first cut missed (the build caught them):
  
  - mach/main.py: drop the telemetry-future callback wiring, the
    init-done/start-time bookkeeping and its shutdown wait. The context
    keeps a NoopTelemetry so command code keeps working.
  - mach/telemetry.py: slimmed to is_telemetry_enabled (kept: mach sentry
    gates crash reporting on it). Invocation reporting, the Glean
    construction, the opt-in prompt and the employee detection go away.
  - mach/telemetry_interface.py: drop the GleanTelemetry class.
  - mozboot/bootstrap.py: drop the first-run telemetry opt-in prompt.
  - build/mach_initialize.py: drop the background telemetry/system-metrics
    startup block, the dispatch finalize hook (which submitted the usage
    ping) and _finalize_telemetry_glean.
  - mozbuild/base.py: the metrics property no longer waits on telemetry
    init (always ready Noop).
  - Delete metrics.yaml/pings.yaml (mach + mozbuild), the generated
    metrics docs, telemetry.md, the two telemetry test modules and their
    python.toml entries.
  
  python/mozbuild build metrics still sink to the Noop Mock and are never
  submitted; the build controller is left untouched on purpose.
  
  [core/71-webrtc-telemetry.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead WebRTC telemetry shells
  
  Remove the dead WebRTC telemetry shells and their whole apparatus.
  Every recording call was already neutered, so this only deletes code
  that computes into the void:
  
  - PeerConnectionImpl: RecordCodec/EndOfCall/SignalingTelemetry defs,
    decls and call sites; StartCallTelem + its connected-state call;
    PeerConnectionAutoTimer, sCallDurationTimers and the mCallTelem*
    members; the orphaned base/histogram.h include.
  - PeerConnectionCtx: RecordCommonRtpTelemetry def and its two
    DeliverStats calls (last-report bookkeeping stays).
  - TransportLayerDtls: the three Record*Telemetry methods, decls, all
    six call sites and the handshakeTelemetryRecorded gate flag.
  
  Left alone on purpose: the per-second stats timer, DeliverStats
  skeleton, mLastReports and conduit telemetry (about:webrtc-adjacent
  plumbing, needs its own dependency pass), and the non-WebRTC media
  recorders (MediaDevices/MediaSource/DecoderData/RemoteDecoder).
